# Regression trace for the screen-0x27 auto-dismiss bug (session 14 of
# project_event_popup_arms): load a save, let the post-load welcome/report
# series (0xc8/0xc9/0xca) run with {"auto_dismiss":1}, then click a map cell
# 3x well after it should have settled.  Load prefix + first click
# coordinate copied verbatim from click_county.jsonl (already proven to
# land on a clickable map cell).
#
# What this caught: ti_dismiss_chip (engine.c) called engine_popup_scroll_
# input_step() without resyncing its `st->screen` from the global after —
# a dismissed scroll opened over screen 0x27 restores the screen via
# engine_set_current_screen() directly (an out-of-band global write), but
# engine_tick_ingame_input_step's post-dispatch write-back
# (`if (st.screen != g_sim_current_screen) engine_set_current_screen(st.
# screen)`) used to stomp that fresh restore right back to the STALE
# pre-dismiss value in the SAME frame — the screen never actually left
# 0x27 and every later hint/click silently dropped.  Fixed by resyncing
# st->screen = g_sim_current_screen at the end of ti_dismiss_chip.
#
# How to check: watch engine_set_current_screen's caller
# (engine_tick_ingame_input_step / engine.c) — before the fix the screen
# gets stuck at 39 (0x27) forever after the first welcome hint; after the
# fix it cycles cleanly through all 3 hints and settles at screen 0. No
# built-in assertion here (this is a live/manual trace, not a host test —
# engine.c isn't part of the host suite) — diff the 'settled' capture's
# screen value, or re-add a temporary printf in engine_set_current_screen
# to watch the transitions.
#
# STILL BLOCKED (separate, deeper issue, not this bug): the 3 clicks below
# don't actually reach engine_army_select in this environment — ti_edge_
# scroll reads g_input_raw_cursor_x/y (populated by a real GetCursorPos()
# poll), which in this headless/WSL environment returns a real desktop
# mouse position disconnected from this trace's synthesized WM_LBUTTONDOWN
# lParam (i.e. the intended (260,250) click coordinate never reaches the
# raw-cursor pipeline), so edge-scroll's "cursor near window edge" hit-
# test sees garbage and consumes every click before army_select ever
# runs. A future frontier: needs either real mouse control in the test
# environment, or reworking the headless seat to feed the synthesized
# coordinate into g_input_raw_cursor_x/y too.
